<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.5.3: Finding Irrational Solutions by Completing the Square</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02410</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.5.3: Finding Irrational Solutions by Completing the Square</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e12a0394-6019-4fe2-8ef3-290c86b12390</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<div class="os-raise-familysupport">
  <para>Access the <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b62c9150250bf52d6cc37569213ab516e0090dca">Desmos guide PDF</link> for tips on solving problems with the Desmos graphing calculator.</para>
</div>
<para>Here is an example of an equation being solved by graphing and by <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">completing the square</term>.</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f2655f0650fd05c200ff9c432bafd8068e71a420"/></media></figure></para>
<para>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}+6 x+7 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}+6 x+9 &amp;=2 \\ (x+3)^{2} &amp;=2 \\ x+3 &amp;=\pm \sqrt{2} \\ x &amp;=-3 \pm \sqrt{2} \end{aligned}\) </para>
<para>Verify: \(\sqrt{2}\) is approximately 1.414. So \(-3+ \sqrt{2} \approx -1.586\) and \(-3- \sqrt{2} \approx -4.414\).</para>
<para>For each equation, find the exact solutions by completing the square and the approximate solutions by graphing. Then, verify that the solutions found using the two methods are close. If you get stuck, refer back to the example.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(x^2+4x+1=0\)</para>
    <para>Find the exact solutions by completing the square.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}+4 x+1 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}+4 x &amp;=-1 \\ x^{2}+4 x+4 &amp;=-1+4 \\ x^{2}+4 x+4 &amp;=3 \\ (x+2)^{2} &amp;=3 \\ \sqrt{(x+2)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{3} \\ x+2 &amp;=\pm \sqrt{3} \\x&amp;=-2 \pm \sqrt{3} \end{aligned}\) </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Graph the equation to find approximate solutions. </item>
</list>
<para>Use the Desmos graphing tool or technology outside the course. </para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem> 
    <para>When you have finished graphing, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/fc7c976f9f84826aaf037e005a96b757fba599c6"/></media></figure></para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="8598f8e0-fb62-4e5e-bf45-9db30d216c6b" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e4b9dc8d-0ea3-4566-af06-451d36647eee" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Are the solutions you found using the two methods close? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes. Solutions were the same: \(x \approx -0.268\) and \(x \approx -3.732\).</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(x^2−10x+18=0\)</para>
    <para>Find the exact solutions by completing the square.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}-10 x+18 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}-10 x &amp;=-18 \\ x^{2}-10 x+25 &amp;=-18+25 \\ x^{2}-10 x+25 &amp;=7 \\ (x-5)^{2} &amp;=7 \\ \sqrt{(x-5)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{7} \\ x-5 &amp;=\pm \sqrt{7} \\ x &amp;=5 \pm \sqrt{7} \end{aligned}\) </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Graph the equation to find approximate solutions. </item>
</list>
<para>Use the Desmos graphing tool or technology outside the course. </para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
  
    <para>When you have finished graphing, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para><figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e68253272f86e5daa2ea0ff1148ead33a54fd788"/></media></figure></para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="3b59c9ac-6cf0-40c5-8cf2-95d34eb9fde0" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q2c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0f0d59d2-2fcd-4daf-ac6a-c1ab9c931506" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Are the solutions you found using the two methods close? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes. Solutions were the same: \(x \approx 7.646\) and \(x \approx 2.354\).</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
