<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(x^2+5x+\frac{1}{4}=0\)</para>
    <para>Find the exact solutions by completing the square.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} x^{2}+5 x+\frac{1}{4} &amp;=&amp; 0 \\ x^{2}+5 x &amp;=&amp; -\frac{1}{4} \\ x^{2}+5 x+\left(\frac{5}{2}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp; -\frac{1}{4}+\left(\frac{5}{2}\right)^{2} \\ x^{2}+5 x+\frac{25}{4} &amp;=&amp; -\frac{1}{4}+\frac{25}{4} \\ x^{2}+5 x+\frac{25}{4} &amp;=&amp; \frac{24}{4} \\ x^{2}+5 x+\frac{25}{4} &amp;=&amp; 6 \\ \left(x+\frac{5}{2}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp; 6 \\ \sqrt{\left(x+\frac{5}{2}\right)^{2}} &amp;=&amp; \sqrt{6} \\ x+\frac{5}{2} &amp;=&amp; \pm \sqrt{6} \\ x &amp;=&amp; -\frac{5}{2} \pm \sqrt{6} \end{array}\) </para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Graph the equation to find approximate solutions. </item>
</list>
<para>Use the Desmos graphing tool or technology outside the course. </para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem> 
    <para>When you have finished graphing, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/78c3ebc4c9c1e4fcbe7e9c7c06eea1266ec14713"/></media></figure></solution></exercise>
</example><div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="b67862a2-4253-47c5-9ca2-8dee5d31972e" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q3c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e91e1f89-ee24-4fd8-a748-9709bcd4de75" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Are the solutions you found using the two methods close?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes. Solutions were the same: \(x \approx -4.949\) and \(x \approx -0.051\).</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
